Use the **art-director** subagent to run the **`visual-craft`** creative canon on $ARGUMENTS:
deconstruct the reference or trend (layout system · hierarchy · focal point · density · signature
move), filter each move through the {{SYSTEM_NAME}} token/brand fence (✅ keep / ✳️ adapt / 🚫 drop / 🧱 DS gap),
deliberately TWEAK what doesn't fit so the result is ours — not a copy — and propose **2–3 named,
distinct directions** with a recommendation.

Return the skill's output: the reference deconstruction · the direction menu (`signature move · layout ·
density · {{SYSTEM_NAME}} components · best-when · tradeoff`) · optional low-fi `Explorations / <flow>` frames ·
the build spec for the chosen direction ({{SYSTEM_NAME}} component list + token calls + layout math) that
**ui-designer** builds pixel-perfect. Recreate ≠ replicate. Aesthetic creativity is in layout /
composition / hierarchy / rhythm / imagery only — a new-component or new-token need is a DS gap, not a
hand-build. Trend never overrides usability or WCAG AA.

Defer to the agent + skill — do not restate the method here.
